\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces GAT-CTDE architecture. (a) A shared Graph Attention encoder over the fully-connected 3-gNB topology produces one embedding per node; per-slice Q-heads, each with its own parameters, consume that node's own embedding row at action-selection time (decentralized execution). (b) The federated training variant: each gNB is a client with a private copy of the same network, synchronized via periodic FedAvg with an optional per-client DP-SGD clip-and-noise step.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{3}{}{}{}}
